WEBVTT

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.510
Start of the Rainy Season

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.220
Um, hello.

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:45.100
Oh, Kiriyama.

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.520
Huh? What's wrong with Hina?

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:50.190
She just has a nosebleed.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:52.320
You're probably surprised
to see her covered in blood.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.070
No, don't look at me!

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.070
Sis, get me a bath towel!

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:56.950
Okay, okay.

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:00.330
This is embarrassing! Don't look at me!

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.330
SNIFF-SNIFF

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.950
There's nothing embarrassing
about a nosebleed.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:06.790
Just calm down.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:15.090
Oh, look at these big peaches!

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.970
How delightful! I love peaches!

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:24.270
There're so many. Weren't they expensive?

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.900
Um, did something happen to Hina?

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:34.730
Kind of, at school...

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.950
It's complicated.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:42.870
Hina...

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.160
Don't look at me!

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.660
<i>And there.</i>

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.840
It's okay. Everybody gets nosebleeds.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.260
It's no big deal.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:56.880
Really?

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:57.800
Yeah.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.180
Do you often get nosebleeds?

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:02.850
Yeah.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.600
Wait, come to think of it...

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.930
REALIZATION

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.690
Sorry. I don't.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:12.900
- I never have.
- You liar! Idiot!

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:19.780
The type that does
as he's told

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:19.780
Trying not to look

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:17.280
I bought some peaches.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.780
But maybe ice cream
would've been better.

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:24.410
Peaches are good. I like peaches.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.290
I see. That's good.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.790
The cat's heavy! Can you move it?

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.040
Oh, okay.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.420
LONG

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:38.130
<i>No, I'm gonna stay here!</i>

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.050
Rei...

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.470
Yes?

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:47.890
Thank you.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.190
Sure.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.980
Well, we're going to the supermarket
for the sale.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.400
Keep lying down for another 20 minutes.

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:00.950
Okay!

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.200
STAMPS
MAIL

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:13.710
About Hina...

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:18.670
Apparently her homeroom teacher
talked to her after school.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:21.970
Why? Why is this happening?

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:26.930
Ms. Kawamoto, why aren't you
getting along with everyone?

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:29.390
"Why aren't I"?

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:32.640
It's always been like this.
I told you then, about Sakura!

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.940
Don't raise your voice to me.

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:38.530
Honestly, Ms. Kawamoto,
why can't you be more cooperative?

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:49.910
<i>Suddenly, everything went red.</i>

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:53.500
<i>It wasn't just because of the sunset.</i>

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:58.800
So until just a little while ago,
she was furious and crying hysterically.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:06.970
She must have been frustrated.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:10.140
My mind went blank too when I heard.

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:12.060
I thought, "How terrible."

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:19.190
<i>Hina...</i>

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:26.320
Maybe I'll get called in for a talk soon, too.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:31.450
I'm the only one at our house who can go.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.160
I wonder if the other girl's parents
will come, too.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:38.250
Can I hold my own against them?

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:40.550
I'm so worried.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:43.590
What'll I do if they turn out to be
those "monster parents" you hear about?

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:46.220
*Sending to you via imaginative video

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:46.220
<i>How dare your kid accuse
our cute daughter like that?</i>

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:48.850
And if that happens...

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:52.560
...should I unleash Monster Grandpa?

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:59.060
What have you done
to my granddaughter, damn it?!

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:03.690
And if that doesn't work...

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:05.360
...there's the ultimate weapon!

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.780
Aunt Misaki!

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.450
Shall we come to an amicable resolution?

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.450
The Shadowy Monster
of Ginza *** Street

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:14.200
One way or another!

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:20.040
What should I do? My alma mater
will be engulfed in a sea of flames!

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.300
Aaaahhhhh

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.300
U-Um, Akari?

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:26.590
It'll be fine.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:31.010
It'll be fine. Hina didn't do anything wrong.

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:35.100
Besides, there are so many people
I can rely on.

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:36.480
I'm sure it'll work out.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:41.730
<i>Her hands...</i>

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:50.740
I'm here too!

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:54.660
HERE TOO

00:06:58.750 --> 00:06:59.870
<i>He yelled!</i>

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:01.840
<i>Dangerous! You're dangerous!</i>

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:04.460
<i>Hey! Who are you?!</i>

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:05.800
GASP

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:11.010
Sorry about this! Quiet, Chibi and Meg!
Sorry to bother you!

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:13.430
Be quiet, Pochi! These people
are in the middle of something!

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:16.350
HERE TOO

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:17.520
PFFT

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:20.770
A-Akari? Are you laughing at me?

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:20.770
WUFF
WUFF

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:20.770
BARK
BARK

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:20.770
RAR
RAR

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:23.270
That was loud.

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:27.780
But...

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:29.900
...thank you.

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:34.030
If something happens...

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:37.040
I'll be counting on you.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:39.160
Okay?

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:45.050
Yes. Of course.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:47.010
I'm ready for anything!

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:52.800
At last! At last, we made it this far.

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:57.970
One more win for both of us
and we'll make it to the finals!

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:03.060
But a powerful enemy is lying in wait for me.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:04.060
Last year's...

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:08.230
No, the Newcomer King
among Newcomer Kings! That man!

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:09.490
NEWCOMER

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:13.320
Because of that regulation for participants
being 5th dan or lower and under 26 years old,

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:17.660
that Junkei Yamazaki has been
the Newcomer King for the last four years!

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:17.660
*Sending to you via imaginative video

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.710
<i>If this keeps up,
he'll be the eternal Newcomer King!</i>

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:21.710
Eternal Newcomer King Celebration

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:28.800
I don't know if that title
would be an honor or dishonor.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.590
It's a dishonor, of course.

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:33.430
To all of us newcomers!

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:38.010
Yeah. Sorry.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:41.310
You're right... for once.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:42.810
<i>Don't say "for once"!</i>

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:47.570
You better not lose either,
to the Irritated Prince of the East!

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.320
Break him into pieces!

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.650
Subaru Hachiya
(5th dan)

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:52.780
He's been doing well lately,
which has made him even more irritated.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:52.780
Personality: The more he wins,
the more irritated he becomes
(three-stage reverse sliding scale)
Attack: Fast Play/Tongue-Clicking
Favorite Pieces: Bishop, Rook

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:54.030
Attack: Fast Play/Tongue-Clicking

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.740
Hachiya, huh? I didn't know.

00:08:56.740 --> 00:08:58.540
I don't like that tongue clicking.

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:01.410
Be careful.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:05.830
Especially right now.
I heard he's gunning for us.

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:06.670
<i>Why?</i>

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:07.790
Why?!

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:13.430
Because you and I are the princes
of the next generation, of course.

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:17.930
He's worried
that we'll steal his princely position!

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:19.100
<i>What's that?</i>

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.930
Don't laugh! It's true!

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:24.390
It even said so in Modern Shogi!

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:25.980
Kiriyama.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:29.860
This is a variation on the Cheerful Rook
from the study group, but...

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:36.360
Silver to 3-2, Silver to 3-7, Pawn to 4-4,

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:42.160
and for Pawn 3-5, Pawn same,
and Silver to 4-6?

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:50.630
Also, a variation to the Bishop Exchange
with the same pattern,

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:54.340
how's Promoted Bishop to 2-8,
Promoted Bishop to 4-4,

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:56.340
and Promoted Bishop to 3-9?

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:04.680
But would Pawn to 2-2, Gold same,
Silver to 3-3 be difficult?

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:09.360
<i>Um, also, uh...</i>

00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:10.320
Nikaidou.

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:12.230
<i>What do you think about Rook to 6-9?</i>

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:13.440
Nikaidou!

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:16.200
You'll be fine.

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:19.320
Kiriyama.

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:24.450
<i>That aside, you're going to Osaka tomorrow
a day early, right?</i>

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:26.370
So go to bed.

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:28.000
<i>Right.</i>

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.790
<i>It's more important for you
right now to stay healthy.</i>

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:33.630
Yeah. Got it.

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:35.800
Thanks.

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:53.610
<i>When I opened the window,</i>

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:56.610
<i>mixed in with the smell of the river,</i>

00:10:59.740 --> 00:11:01.280
<i>was the scent of rain.</i>

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:06.620
<i>What is Hina doing right now?</i>

00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:11.000
<i>Is she able to sleep all right?</i>

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:14.500
<i>I'll be counting on you.</i>

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:18.760
<i>Even when I do my best, I go nowhere.</i>

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:23.760
<i>I can't do what normal people can do.</i>

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:27.850
<i>I want to help.</i>

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:32.690
<i>And yet, I don't know how I can be helpful.</i>

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:39.070
<i>But, I have no way of being helpful,
other than this.</i>

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:42.030
<i>So I want to win.</i>

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:44.030
<i>I want to win.</i>

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:46.330
<i>I want to win.</i>

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:51.170
<i>Even if it's just with one thing,
I want to be strong for them.</i>

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:53.460
<i>That's right.</i>

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:55.460
<i>I...</i>

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:58.340
<i>...want to be needed.</i>

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:02.970
Start of the Rainy Season

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:06.970
Hachiya

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:38.380
<i>If something happens, Ill be counting on you.</i>

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:03.910
<i>At that time, when Akari's cheeks and voice
were lit up by the setting sun...</i>

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:12.290
<i>I can't get them out of my head.</i>

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:18.920
<i>For the first time, I feel desire for something.</i>

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:26.510
<i>And it isn't an innocent desire.</i>

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:30.970
<i>Whether that's a good thing or a bad thing...</i>

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:34.100
<i>...I don't know.</i>

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:37.980
<i>Nevertheless...</i>

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:41.280
<i>...I want to win right now.</i>

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:44.110
<i>I want to win, no matter what.</i>

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:50.120
<i>The Newcomer Tournament semi-finals...</i>

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:52.500
<i>If I win this match, I'll go on to the finals.</i>

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:54.000
<i>My opponent is...</i>

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:02.010
Don't stomp around, Hachi.

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:03.260
Sorry.

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:12.020
<i>Subaru Hachiya, 5th-Dan.
Twenty-three years old, Class C-1.</i>

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:16.190
<i>Out of all the professional shogi players
in their 20s, he's the most promising.</i>

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:21.440
<i>He's trained at his workshop to become good
at playing fast and aggressively.</i>

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:22.820
<i>Tongue-clicking.</i>

00:14:25.450 --> 00:14:26.740
<i>Shaking his legs.</i>

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:28.990
<i>Tapping his folding fan.</i>

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:33.240
<i>His nickname is the Irritated Prince of the East.</i>

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:38.880
<i>In this world, strength is everything.</i>

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:41.880
<i>If you're strong,
everything will become justified.</i>

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:47.010
It's now 10:00. Please begin.

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:49.010
Let's have a good game.

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:51.930
<i>But...</i>

00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:00.650
<i>...it kind of bugs me.</i>

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:20.790
<i>A Cheerful Central Rook, huh?</i>

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:23.340
<i>So he intends to come at me hard and fast.</i>

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:34.390
<i>I'll take this challenge.</i>

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:41.860
<i>That was fast!</i>

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:56.200
<i>He really plays fast.
Makes me wonder if it's on purpose.</i>

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:01.750
TAP TAP
TAP
TAP TAP
TAPTAPTAP

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:01.750
<i>And he's noisy.</i>

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:08.340
TAP
TAPTAP
TAP TAP TAP
TAPTAP

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:06.210
<i>I can't let it get to me though.</i>

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:08.340
<i>It'll make it harder to focus.</i>

00:17:47.110 --> 00:17:48.860
<i>His defense is strong on the side.</i>

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:53.240
<i>So that means I just have to go from above.</i>

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:06.500
<i>If that's what he'll do,
then I'll go Knight to 8-6.</i>

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:21.720
<i>Fast play, tongue-clicking, leg-shaking...</i>

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.430
<i>How can I put it?</i>

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:30.980
<i>Does he have to do all this to play shogi?</i>

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:41.330
<i>How can he think it's okay to behave like this?</i>

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:47.580
<i>How can he sit there and not think about
how his opponent will take it?</i>

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:51.630
<i>An edge pawn?</i>

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:53.710
<i>"Against the Edge King, push the Edge Pawn"?</i>

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:56.470
<i>Like that'll do the trick?</i>

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:05.480
<i>The freedom must be nice, behaving as you like
without sensing the other person's mood.</i>

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:08.900
<i>He's so slow it's getting me irritated.</i>

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:14.530
<i>As long as I've got a dragon in this row,
I'm going to be faster.</i>

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:17.030
<i>Annoying.</i>

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:19.530
<i>Man, he's annoying.</i>

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:25.040
<i>It's like I can hear the voices in his head.</i>

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:32.710
<i>I bet he thinks the world revolves around him.</i>

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:45.220
<i>H-He's sacrificing his bishop?</i>

00:19:46.060 --> 00:19:47.430
<i>What?</i>

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:50.940
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:55.150
<i>BISHOP</i>

00:19:55.530 --> 00:19:57.280
<i>I can't afford not to take it.</i>

00:19:57.740 --> 00:20:02.530
<i>But if I take it, I'll be one row off.
Then the edge will be...</i>

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:07.410
<i>He'll be able to swing the edge?</i>

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:09.910
<i>Where did I make a mistake?</i>

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:12.880
<i>Where was it? I didn't see that Bishop coming.</i>

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:17.380
<i>Is he going to checkmate me?
No. A faster move...</i>

00:20:18.210 --> 00:20:19.380
<i>Isn't there a fast move?</i>

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:22.590
<i>An even faster move?</i>

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:32.230
I lost...

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:43.280
Noisy...

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:47.240
If he'll get a bad temper when he loses,
he should play more slowly.

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:50.910
Kiriyama!

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:54.130
You did a lousy job
removing that "bee's nest!"

00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:56.130
You made him buzz even louder!

00:20:56.130 --> 00:20:58.000
Be more cognizant
of the other players around you!

00:20:58.130 --> 00:20:59.800
Wait a second, me?!

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:02.300
Who suddenly starts poking the hive
with a stick?

00:21:02.300 --> 00:21:03.970
That was on purpose, wasn't it?

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:07.640
There're a lot of other ways to deal with it,
like wrap it in a bag and fumigate it!

00:21:07.640 --> 00:21:09.390
BUZZ BUZZ BUZZ BUZZ

00:21:09.470 --> 00:21:11.140
I-It's my fault?

00:21:11.230 --> 00:21:15.150
That Hachiya-bee is always buzzing!
He has been since elementary school!

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:18.400
It's too late to change him now!
So we've all given up! Got it?!

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:21.360
All you can do is bag him
before he starts to buzz! Geez!

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:23.490
As you get older, it's harder to focus.

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:27.030
So be more considerate!
We were playing an important match here!

00:21:27.030 --> 00:21:28.910
The next term's seed is on the line!

00:21:28.910 --> 00:21:32.790
When you're older, it's tough
starting a tournament from square one! Get it?

00:21:32.790 --> 00:21:35.670
I really want to make it past this round!
I lost though!

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:37.880
Uh, okay.

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:40.510
Everyone's so noisy buzzing around.

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:42.300
Sheesh, youngsters these days.

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:46.510
Hachi is too easy to understand,
but Kiriyama, you're too hard to understand!

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:50.890
You should live so you're easier to understand.
Like Hachi.

00:21:50.890 --> 00:21:52.850
After all, you're both similar on the inside.

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:55.400
Please don't compare me to him. I'm not—

00:21:55.400 --> 00:21:56.770
You are like him!

00:21:57.020 --> 00:21:59.940
You think the world
revolves around you, don't you?

00:22:01.610 --> 00:22:04.150
Why? What?!

00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:06.160
SLAM

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:09.160
Well, shall we head out?

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:11.160
Good luck, Kiriyama.

00:22:11.450 --> 00:22:14.910
Hang in there.
This is where Hachi really takes his time.

00:22:14.910 --> 00:22:15.870
See you!

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:19.500
Okay, the post-mortem...

00:22:19.670 --> 00:22:22.920
GRIND GRIND GRIND

00:22:19.670 --> 00:22:22.920
RUMBLE RUMBLE RUMBLE

00:22:20.460 --> 00:22:22.710
Let's make it a thorough one!

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:24.170
KYAAAAA

00:22:24.420 --> 00:22:27.590
<i>Tongue-clicking. Leg-shaking. An attitude.</i>

00:22:27.840 --> 00:22:31.140
<i>Despite displaying all of these things,
he's surprisingly loved.</i>

00:22:30.640 --> 00:22:34.430
TEAR TRACKS

00:22:31.140 --> 00:22:33.980
<i>Subaru Hachiya, 5th-Dan, 23 years old.</i>

00:22:35.810 --> 00:22:37.690
TAPTAP
TAP TAP TAP
TAP

00:22:39.860 --> 00:22:42.860
<i>Even after that, Hachi hung around Kiriyama</i>

00:22:43.230 --> 00:22:46.820
and made him engage in a post-mortem
at a family restaurant until the wee hours of the night.

00:22:47.240 --> 00:22:48.780
<i>As the world revolved around him,</i>

00:22:48.780 --> 00:22:50.080
<i>"I can't understand it."</i>

00:22:50.080 --> 00:22:53.120
<i>He yelled that a million times.</i>

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:53.120
<i>GOBBLE GOBBLE
TAP TAP TAP</i>

00:22:53.370 --> 00:22:56.410
<i>We're not alike! We're nothing alike at all!</i>

00:22:57.670 --> 00:23:00.040
Hachiya

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.010
Next Episode Preview

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:37.640
Episode 30

00:24:32.340 --> 00:24:35.180
What the hell is that?!

00:24:35.720 --> 00:24:37.640
But this is a school!

00:24:37.850 --> 00:24:39.100
I lack knowledge.

00:24:39.100 --> 00:24:41.390
You're just a second-year
high school student.

00:24:41.390 --> 00:24:42.600
I'm not useful!

00:24:42.600 --> 00:24:44.020
I'm a teacher!

00:24:44.020 --> 00:24:45.150
I did my best...

00:24:45.150 --> 00:24:47.190
Don't underestimate a teacher!

00:24:47.530 --> 00:24:50.030
So please teach me, Mr. Hayashida!

00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:58.750
ILLUSTRATION:
RIEKO NISHIHARA

00:24:51.360 --> 00:24:55.330
Kiriyama, you're not thinking
of going home soon, are you?

00:24:55.330 --> 00:24:58.080
Excuse me! One more parfait!
